SOAPBOX: This was another last minute remote operation from NX6T in Fallbrook, 
SOAPBOX: Ca. (aka "NashVille"), although I was in the SF Bay Area at the time.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: Everything checked out before hand except I didn't check WINKEY's 
SOAPBOX: keying of the radio; which I discovered (at 12:05z) it could not 
SOAPBOX: do as the COM4 serial port was out and no one for miles available 
SOAPBOX: to see if the cable fell out or if there was some other problem.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: The solution was macro/keyboard keying by the RCForb remote access software.
SOAPBOX: After awhile I became comfortable enough with jumping between the VNC viewer
SOAPBOX: screen (to log under N1MM+)and RCForb to key the transmitter.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: I purposely ran increasing amounts of high power to verify a new air
SOAPBOX: conditioning system for the shack was working properly.  
SOAPBOX: When it gets too hot STN-1's Toshiba laptop overheats and shuts itself off.  
SOAPBOX: This weekend after rebooting the laptop (in a hopeless attempt to revive COM4),
SOAPBOX: the computer itself operated flawlessly; although I can't necessarily make that
SOAPBOX: claim about the operator.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: I loved hearing all the EA stations.  I only wish there had been 5X as many.
SOAPBOX: 40 meters was WIDE OPEN to Spain, so the lack of Spanish participation surprised me.
SOAPBOX: 
SOAPBOX: You can read my write-up about this Gig in the WQ6X Contest BLOG:
SOAPBOX: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.Com
NAME: Ron Fitch (WQ6X)
